# Sense TTS Podcast — Environment Variables

Copy this file to `~/.env` (recommended) or set as system environment variables.

```bash
# ============================================================
# Tavily Search API (required)
# Get your key: https://app.tavily.com/home
#
# Multi-key round-robin: comma-separate several keys and each run picks one
# at random, spreading quota across them. Blank entries are ignored, so
# stray commas and spaces are harmless.
#   TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-11111,tvly-22222,tvly-33333
# ============================================================
TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-your_key_here

# ============================================================
# SenseAudio TTS (required, PAID service)
# Get your token: https://docs.senseaudio.cn  (SenseTime SenseAudio)
#
# Bearer token for POST https://api.senseaudio.cn/v1/t2a_v2.
# Billing is per synthesized character — a medium podcast (~2500 chars)
# costs roughly 2500 characters of quota per full run. Regenerate single
# lines with `python scripts/tts.py <workdir> --line N` instead of
# re-running everything.
# ============================================================
SENSE_AUDIO_TOKEN=your_senseaudio_token_here

# ============================================================
# SenseAudio WEB channel (optional — enables scripts/web_tts.py)
#
# Browser-session token from the senseaudio.cn console ("语音应用 →
# 文本转语音"). The web channel exposes 74 voices / 167 labels (incl.
# 限免 SVIP ones the API rejects) and is usually free during promotions,
# at the cost of token fragility: it expires in ~60 days and rotates on
# every re-login. Grab it via: log in → F12 → Network → audition any
# voice → copy the `authorization` header (the part after "Bearer ")
# from the api/voice/tts request.
#
# Segments are saved as native WAV (lossless); concat.py performs the
# single final MP3 encode, which needs `pip install lameenc`. The lossless
# podcast.wav master is kept alongside podcast.mp3 either way.
# ============================================================
# SENSE_WEB_TOKEN=v2.public.eyJ...

# ============================================================
# Optional
# ============================================================
# TTS model override (default: sensenova-tts-2.0)
# SENSE_TTS_MODEL=sensenova-tts-2.0
```

## Verification

Check the API-channel backend (verifies the token and lists visible voices):
```bash
python scripts/tts.py --check
# Full end-to-end probe (synthesizes 3 chars, consumes a tiny bit of quota):
python scripts/tts.py --check --probe
```

Check the web-channel backend (verifies SENSE_WEB_TOKEN, lists web voices):
```bash
python scripts/web_tts.py --check
```

Check Tavily configuration:
```bash
bash scripts/search.sh --check
# Windows:
powershell -NoProfile -File scripts/search.ps1 -Check
```

## Loading Priority

All scripts in this skill load environment variables in this order:

| Priority | Source |
|----------|--------|
| 1 | System environment variable (`export KEY=val` / `$env:KEY`) |
| 2 | `~/.env` file (standard `KEY=VALUE` lines) |
